{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"TRACKER CONVERTED to a STANDALONE CLONE (approved maintenance window).\n\nBefore: .tickets-tracker was a LINKED WORKTREE — gitdir pointed into\n/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.git/worktrees/-tickets-tracker, sharing one .git (and therefore ONE\nstash stack) with 11 source worktrees. That sharing is the mechanism behind this bug.\nAfter: .git is a real directory — own index, own refs, own stash stack (0 entries). A stash\ncreated in any source worktree can no longer be popped into the ticket store.\n\nThis matches production: infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:154 already creates the reviewbot's\nstore with 'git clone --single-branch --branch tickets'. The dev machine was the outlier.\n\nPROCEDURE (worth encoding in the maintenance entrypoint AC):\n  1. rebar bridge pause '<reason>'   — durable pause, so nothing recreates the worktree\n  2. quiet check: tracker HEAD stable over 20s (a writer recreated it during an earlier\n     attempt and committed events mid-restructure — that attempt was aborted)\n  3. verify 0 unpushed and 0 unmerged; FLUSH anything pending first (a pending\n     'ticket: COMPACT' commit had to be merged + pushed before proceeding)\n  4. move the worktree aside (reversible), git worktree prune\n  5. clone the tickets branch STANDALONE\n  6. carry over the git-ignored LOCAL store state, which a fresh clone does not have:\n       .env-id (environment identity stamped into every event — MUST be preserved for\n       continuity, not regenerated), .ensure-applied, .opcert-key + .opcert-key.pub (operator\n       signing key, 0600), .graph-cache.json\n  7. verify read AND write, then rebar bridge resume\n\nTWO TRAPS FOUND THE HARD WAY:\n  - Cloning from the LOCAL repo FAILS: this checkout is a PARTIAL (promisor) clone and cannot\n    serve a full clone ('could not fetch ... from promisor remote'). Clone from the REMOTE.\n    This failed with the store already moved aside, i.e. mid-outage.\n  - A fresh clone is NOT a working store: writes fail with 'ticket system not initialized'\n    until .env-id (and the opcert key, for signing) are carried over. Reads work fine, so the\n    breakage is invisible until the first write."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786336164440375001,"uuid":"b42358b0-75d8-475a-a188-21814e668e5e"}